## VACUITY READ — all 34 new theorem statements (CX-P11a self-read, 2026-10-20)
Each conclusion was read for every disjunct: NONE of these conclusions contains an escape disjunction. Existentials below name a concrete derivation, successor, relation or recorded evidence; none is an unbounded collision predicate. Concrete examples are affirmative/negative tests, not universal theorems with impossible hypotheses. Existing landed signatures remain byte-identical. No independent reader is claimed.
- WorldsField.derives_in_model: arbitrary reduct derivation maps into any model; conclusion is membership, requires real rule-closure induction, no escape.
- WorldsField.stable_iff_labelling: independently defined reduct semantics versus model closure + no unfounded IN subset; reverse direction uses the underived-IN set, not an alias or P→P.
- WorldsField.admissibleWorlds_eq_stableLabellings: completed executable analyzer equals the canonical independent labellings; exact completion/canonical restrictions inherited, no new landed premise.
- WorldsField.cycle_unfounded: actual withdrawn reduct/proposal and set {1,2}; false body 0 is excluded, cycle edges supply support internal to the set. No empty set premise.
- WorldsField.unfounded_cycle_not_labelling: the explicit proposal contains 1, so unfounded exclusion genuinely fails; no vacuous antecedent.
- WorldsField.union_not_labelling: concrete union fails independent stable labelling, consuming the landed stable-model counterexample.
- Interfaces.alternatingSimulation_iff_definition14: both independently written relation conditions, including reverse input successors; requires deterministic input matching, not just enabled labels.
- Interfaces.refines_iff_definition14: same pointed relation witness preserved with exact Def14 equivalence; no weakened existential of unrelated states.
- Interfaces.product_matching: actual synchronized implementation step yields a same-labelled specification step, related successors, and preserved peer compatibility; none of the conjuncts is an escape.
- Interfaces.substitutivity: arbitrary refinement plus compatible peer yields replacement compatibility AND an initialized successor-closed product relation; no vacuous choice of empty relation (initial pair required).
- Interfaces.seven_peer_compatible: every finite horizon, both replies, repeated request/reply; nonempty adversarial peer outputs inhabit safety obligations.
- Interfaces.seven_peer_survives: uses actual generic substitution theorem with more accepted prices/fewer replies; nonempty repeated peer prevents trivial empty-session result.
- Interfaces.enabling_alone_insufficient: concrete initial inclusions AND failure after second input; not disjunctive failure or assumed non-refinement.
- Games.solved_exclusive: inductive win/loss evidence cannot coexist; conclusion negates opposite result, no impossible generic premise (sink/accepted examples inhabit derivations).
- Games.trap_unsolved: nonempty successor and closure assumptions imply absence of either finite derivation; root membership explicit, loop witnesses inhabit assumptions.
- Games.checkDraw_sound: Boolean checker yields independent neither-won-nor-lost semantics; three checks replayed, not a returned tag premise.
- Games.outside_draw_sound: actual returned status binds exact region, establishes successful check and independent Draw; no inference from procedureLimit.
- Games.loop_is_draw: executed self-loop checker AND independent Draw, concrete inhabited trap.
- Games.sink_is_not_draw: executed refusal AND genuine losing derivation; catches missing nonsink check.
- Games.escape_is_not_draw: executed refusal AND genuine winning derivation; catches missing successor-closure check.
- Games.unrelated_loop_is_not_draw: executed refusal AND genuine losing root; catches missing root coverage.
- NogoodGames.accepted_wins: actual declared-domain member accepted by question yields game win, independent of retained candidates/certificates.
- NogoodGames.excluded_loses: all DECLARED members rejected yields game loss; a retained-search absence premise would be insufficient and is absent.
- NogoodGames.checkCertificate_sound: coverage returns exact certificate row, recorded nogood membership, support inclusion, current rejection for each declared member; no disjunction; nonempty positive example inhabits.
